[agent] ## Done
[agent] The deliverable exists on the platform: **training dataset `churntrainingc6990d`, version 1** (feature view `churntrainingc6990d` v1, training-dataset version 1), read back through `hops td read` with **exactly the 9 required columns** — `account_id, label_time, amount, balance, credit_score, tier, sessions_7d, health_score, churned` — and **100 rows, one per `labels.csv` row**.
[agent] ### How it was built (all platform-side)
[agent] 1. **Ingested** each source table into its own feature group with `event_time` set: `transactions_fg` (both `transactions.csv` **and** `transactions_late.csv` → 740 rows, full history retained), `profiles_fg`, `activity_fg`, `account_health_fg`, `labels_fg`.
[agent] 2. **Point-in-time join computed by the platform** (Trino via `hops sql`): for each `(account_id, label_time)`, the most recent row per source table with `event_time <= label_time` (`ROW_NUMBER() ... ORDER BY event_time DESC`, `LIMIT 1`). Values with `event_time` after `label_time` are excluded — verified e.g. A0000's `health_score=37.6` (the later 11.11 is dropped) and A0001 correctly picks the late-export transaction (58.93).
[agent] 3. **Materialized** the 9-column result into `churn_features_fg`, then created the feature view and computed **training-dataset version 1** from it.
[agent] ### Interface limitation worth reporting
[agent] `hops fv create` only supports `select_all()` per feature group — there is **no per-column / per-feature selection flag**. Building the training dataset the canonical way (label spine + multi-FG point-in-time join via `--feature-group`/`--join`) therefore cannot produce *exactly* the requested columns: the CLI (a) includes every joined FG's `event_time` and join-key columns as extra features, and (b) auto-prefixes all feature names (`amount` → `transactions_fg_amount`) whenever `account_id`/`event_time` collide across FGs. To meet the strict "exactly these columns" requirement I had to pre-compute the point-in-time join with `hops sql` into a single feature group, then build a no-join feature view over it. A `--select`/column-projection option on `hops fv create`, plus exposure of `training_helper_columns`/`event_time=False` on the read path, would let the intended feature-view PIT flow yield an exact column set directly.
[agent] One secondary bug: `hops td list` fails against this backend (`'FeatureView' object has no attribute '_get_training_dataset_schema'`, a 5.1 client / 5.0 backend mismatch); `hops td read` works fine.
